# This is the capture that first confirmed the PulseDaemon.setCap() hang hypothesis (STATUS.md,
# AutoTDP-tick-loop investigation, 2026-07-27): 4 TICK-SKIP diagnostic lines (autoActive=false,
# pre-engage), then the release()-write sequence (cpu2/3/4 online=1, then the combined
# policy0/2/5 min/max freq write) at ~22:35:47-48, then total silence for the rest of the
# session -- zero governor write, zero PulseDaemon log, matching a hang inside
# PulseDaemon.setCap()'s unbounded FIFO write (fixed same session, see PulseDaemon.kt).
# Kept: the TICK-SKIP/PulseDaemon lines, the actual chmod/echo write commands, service-start
# markers, and the SELinux AVC denials for com.kei.pulse's own xsu access. Cut: hundreds of
# routine telemetry 'cat' reads (already characterized in STATUS.md as confirming the poll
# loop was alive) and unrelated system noise.
# ---
